    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1038/ngeo1955",
    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Global methane cycle",
    "problem": "The factors responsible for observed decadal changes in atmospheric methane\u2014specifically its stabilization in the early 2000s and renewed rise after 2006\u2014remain unclear because the relative contributions of its various sources and sinks are highly uncertain and poorly constrained by existing models and measurements.",
    "method": "This study constructs decadal methane budgets by combining top-down (atmospheric inversions) and bottom-up (process models and inventories) approaches to quantify global sources and sinks from 1980-2010 and to build scenarios explaining observed atmospheric variability.",
    "task": "The task is to construct decadal budgets for global methane sources and sinks from 1980 to 2010, synthesizing atmospheric measurements and model results to explain the observed stabilization and renewed rise of atmospheric methane levels.",
